<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements for a future Developer ID signature of this .NET +
  Avalonia + SkiaSharp app. Used only on the signed/notarized path in
  build/build-mac.sh (MAC_SIGN_P12 set); the default ad-hoc build does not apply
  entitlements. Each entry is here for a concrete reason:

   - com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit
       The .NET runtime JIT-compiles IL at run time.
   - com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory
       The CoreCLR maps writable+executable memory for the JIT and for
       ready-to-run fixups; without this the hardened runtime kills the process.
   - com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation
       The app loads native libraries that are not signed by the same Team ID
       (libSkiaSharp.dylib, libHarfBuzzSharp.dylib, libAvaloniaNative.dylib and
       the other .NET/Avalonia native assets). Library validation would otherwise
       refuse them.
   - com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables
       The apphost/runtime may rely on DYLD_* during launch; harmless and avoids
       edge-case launch failures under the hardened runtime. (Microsoft's .NET
       notarization guide asks an apphost to keep at least these four.)
   - com.apple.security.automation.apple-events
       The foreground probe reads the browser address bar with osascript. Under
       the hardened runtime, macOS attributes those Apple Events to this app and
       refuses them (error -1743, no prompt) unless it carries this entitlement;
       the prompt text is NSAppleEventsUsageDescription in Info.plist.

  NOT sandboxed: the agent needs Screen Recording and to read the foreground
  window across apps, which the App Sandbox forbids. Distribution is Developer ID
  (direct download), not the Mac App Store, so no com.apple.security.app-sandbox.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
